02:21:12.763 --> 02:21:19.203
<v Clips>But I haven't seen anything even close to the amount of outrage and protests

02:21:19.203 --> 02:21:21.383
<v Clips>and resistance that happened after 2016.

02:21:21.883 --> 02:21:28.743
<v Clips>And I think that really bodes very poorly for us, Especially since Trump has

02:21:28.743 --> 02:21:32.783
<v Clips>no guardrails this time around and it could very well be a lot worse.

02:21:33.023 --> 02:21:38.583
<v Clips>So I don't know. I kind of think that people are too burnt out and too exhausted

02:21:38.583 --> 02:21:41.163
<v Clips>and too depleted to really organize.

02:21:41.263 --> 02:21:43.303
<v Clips>And there's also like...

02:21:43.700 --> 02:21:48.320
<v Clips>A lot of leftist inviting that is also sort of contributing to it and finger pointing.

02:21:48.600 --> 02:21:51.560
<v Clips>Well, also, it's a different platform landscape, right? I feel like Twitter

02:21:51.560 --> 02:21:55.580
<v Clips>generally, especially in the early days of the last Trump presidency,

02:21:56.100 --> 02:22:01.040
<v Clips>played such a key role for activists, even with the Black Lives Matter movement

02:22:01.040 --> 02:22:02.240
<v Clips>or all of these movements, right?

02:22:02.340 --> 02:22:05.820
<v Clips>Like they really emerged on Twitter and I would say sort of solidified on Twitter

02:22:05.820 --> 02:22:10.840
<v Clips>in ways. Und jetzt Twitter hat sich komplett co-optet, obviously, von Elon Musk.

02:22:10.940 --> 02:22:13.920
<v Clips>Ich meine, er hat es. Und pro-Trump-Messagin, in einer Weise,

02:22:13.980 --> 02:22:17.400
<v Clips>dass ich nicht kann, wie es die gleichen Hub für Activism ist.

02:22:17.980 --> 02:22:23.640
<v Wolfgang>Twitter ist tot für Aktivismus, also für linken Aktivismus. Das stellen sie

02:22:23.640 --> 02:22:25.900
<v Wolfgang>erstmal fest. Ich glaube, da würden wir alle nicht widersprechen.

02:22:26.140 --> 02:22:29.440
<v Stefan>Aber wir haben ein neues Twitter. Ja, Blue Sky. Fühlt sich genau an,

02:22:29.520 --> 02:22:33.080
<v Stefan>wie es genau das ist, was ich immer wieder gesucht habe, jetzt seit Elon Musk das gekauft hat.

02:22:33.800 --> 02:22:39.180
<v Stefan>Schon allein, weil es jetzt mit Zill so ein Nassel gibt, wo du einfach deinen

02:22:39.180 --> 02:22:42.140
<v Stefan>Account zur Verfügung stellst und der sucht dann für dich die Links raus,

02:22:42.780 --> 02:22:48.560
<v Stefan>die deine, also den Dufoils und deren Blase sozusagen, das ist so toll,

02:22:48.720 --> 02:22:53.340
<v Stefan>also steigt sozusagen auch den IQ der Salonlektüren jetzt wieder,

02:22:53.580 --> 02:22:56.680
<v Stefan>dadurch, dass wir jetzt wieder mit Blue Sky endlich mal eine Alternative haben.

02:22:56.900 --> 02:23:00.640
<v Wolfgang>Ich bin gespannt. Jetzt spricht DJ Dixon über TikTok.

02:23:08.580 --> 02:23:14.720
<v Clips>I would even go so far as to say that the entire social media ecosystem has

02:23:14.720 --> 02:23:18.040
<v Clips>been radicalized to a pretty significant degree by the right.

02:23:18.200 --> 02:23:21.920
<v Clips>Even if you look on ostensibly leftist or leftist skewing.

02:23:22.740 --> 02:23:28.100
<v Clips>Platforms like TikTok, it basically prioritizes the content that you are most

02:23:28.100 --> 02:23:31.320
<v Clips>likely to engage with and the content that you're most likely to find interesting.

02:23:31.520 --> 02:23:37.100
<v Clips>So it just sort of perpetuates this echo chamber that is happening on the left

02:23:37.100 --> 02:23:40.580
<v Clips>and on the right, regardless of what your political affiliation is.

02:23:40.920 --> 02:23:43.520
<v Wolfgang>Das ist deine Argumentation, die wir eben schon mal gehört haben.

02:23:43.620 --> 02:23:47.420
